--
Constructor variant of cpp17_template_arg_completed_later: the stale
incomplete-base instance reaches symex and aborts an invariant in
symex_assign (SIGABRT) rather than erroring in the front end.
Investigated 2026-07-28: a staleness-remark mechanism
(#had_incomplete_arg on the instance, re-elaboration at the later
point of instantiation) re-runs the instantiation but the re-run
never rebuilds the BASE list (bases()=0 across all elaborations): the
template's stored declaration loses the base-clause information after
the first instantiation, so re-elaboration needs the body/base-clause
preserved first.  Deeper than the cache policy.
